  "authority": "Typed source inspection and implementation only; no new native analysis or runtime validation.",
  "production_dependency": "require_loader_attach_runtime Resources: explicit source-owned completion/reap/worker-return selection; mandatory real external drain retained.",
  "implementation": [
    "LifecycleMode::Explicit remains the default and still requires all four callbacks. SourceOwned must be explicitly selected, rejects a custom owner selector and retains exact own/null completion owners; foreign scheduler owners are rejected.",
    "Actual Application::after_completion already reaps and delivers eligible prepared results. Actual Application::worker_returned and Policy context-finish/one-return checks remain in place. SourceOwned does not install empty after/returned functions; optional observers are preserved.",
    "select_source_worker_lifecycle selects only an unselected profile that already supplies external_drained. It does not install Stop, fabricate external proof or construct per-image lifetime ownership.",
    "SourceOwned gates the outside-Parent external proof on local IO allocations/pending/active calls, accept projections/pending/active calls, application sessions/jobs/active calls and scheduler work/completion queue. The same local guard runs after the opaque proof. A true proof that introduces tracked work cannot attest drain.",
    "Local counters are prerequisites only, never kernel/foreign callback/code/CRT lifetime proof. General Parent allocations and graph event buffers are intentionally left to existing subsequent graph retirement; they are not an external-proof prerequisite.",
    "Existing Graph/Profile/Runtime closure, prepared-job receipt, provider-lease, actual packet and Stop checks remain required. Both production loader hooks remain undefined."
  ],
  "source_scenarios_added": [
    "Passive source-profile validation; reject missing external proof, mixed owner selector and unknown enum mode.",
    "Actual Policy/Profile fixture: preserve own/null completion, reap and worker return without observer callbacks.",
    "Live IO or scheduler work prevents external proof invocation; idle state cannot override false proof; true proof introducing tracked IO remains unaccepted.",
    "Resources selector preflight: absent proof and repeat selection rejected without installing fake lifecycle callbacks."
  ],
  "scenario_limit": "Existing full owning Resources/three-worker driver retains Explicit mode. New SourceOwned Policy/Profile and selector scenarios are source only; none were compiled or executed.",
  "host_layout_change": "Lifecycle gains a by-value enum field. Options/Graph/Worker consumers require a consistent rebuild only when explicitly authorized; no original native ABI compatibility is claimed.",
